{
    "type": "game",
    "name": "Lean Simulator: Desperation",
    "steam_appid": 2936620,
    "required_age": 0,
    "is_free": false,
    "detailed_description": "<span class=\"bb_img_ctn\"><img class=\"bb_img\" src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/2936620/extras/7bd3e856960afd92e7b247a2703dc351.avif?t=1730941997\" width=500 height=150 /></span><br>Lean Simulator: Desperation is a fusion of the Clicker and Survival genres. <br><br>At a surface level this is a meme game but under that unfunny purple coating, you'll find this is a (relatively tame) horror game.<br>There are monsters after you. You need to click fast and be prepared to adapt to new situations to survive as long as possible.<br><br><span class=\"bb_img_ctn\"><img class=\"bb_img\" src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/2936620/extras/9287c05d3030cac8450951f3e73fe680.avif?t=1730941997\" width=500 height=150 /></span><br>The Lean Monsters seek 1 thing: Lean. <br>That's all, provide them Lean and they'll leave you alone.<br>To acquire Lean, simply provide fuel to the Lean Machean by spamming the button attached to it and you will start acquiring Lean over time. <br>Just make sure to keep the Lean Machean fueled and Stabilised.<br><br><span class=\"bb_img_ctn\"><img class=\"bb_img\" src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/2936620/extras/1766eaae9e401dff7888a96f672c533d.avif?t=1730941997\" width=500 height=150 /></span><br>Feeling thirsty? There's a Cuboid of Lean in the room with you that will never run out.<br>Drink from it whenever your vision starts blurring. Difficulty to focus is a sign of Dehydration.<br>Make sure not to drink too much though as Lean is highly addictive.<br><br><span class=\"bb_img_ctn\"><img class=\"bb_img\" src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/2936620/extras/c85b533568ebcbfd9d5e44d91252c857.avif?t=1730941997\" width=500 height=150 /></span><br>Thankfully, you aren't doing this for free. The Lean Monsters will pay you in Bread for giving them Lean.<br>You can use Bread to Upgrade your Lean Quality, or Output Quantity. <br>You can also use it to re-stabilise the Lean Machean in the event it destabilises too far.<br><br>You could also re-stabilise the Lean Machean manually by accessing a hatch next to it but it's recommended to save that for emergencies as you cannot defend yourself while performing Maintenance.<br><br><span class=\"bb_img_ctn\"><img class=\"bb_img\" src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/2936620/extras/1bb06c6d9e8fc583ed1899bba4c8516f.avif?t=1730941997\" width=500 height=150 /></span>:<br>PTSD is an acronym for Potential to Stack Dough, it represents how far you've come since the beginning of the game.<br>The better you perform in a single run, the more PTSD you will earn to spend on making future runs easier.<br>It is essential that you make full use of your PTSD, as you'll need to be prepared for whatever the next run might throw at you.",
    "about_the_game": "<span class=\"bb_img_ctn\"><img class=\"bb_img\" src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/2936620/extras/7bd3e856960afd92e7b247a2703dc351.avif?t=1730941997\" width=500 height=150 /></span><br>Lean Simulator: Desperation is a fusion of the Clicker and Survival genres. <br><br>At a surface level this is a meme game but under that unfunny purple coating, you'll find this is a (relatively tame) horror game.<br>There are monsters after you. You need to click fast and be prepared to adapt to new situations to survive as long as possible.<br><br><span class=\"bb_img_ctn\"><img class=\"bb_img\" src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/2936620/extras/9287c05d3030cac8450951f3e73fe680.avif?t=1730941997\" width=500 height=150 /></span><br>The Lean Monsters seek 1 thing: Lean. <br>That's all, provide them Lean and they'll leave you alone.<br>To acquire Lean, simply provide fuel to the Lean Machean by spamming the button attached to it and you will start acquiring Lean over time. <br>Just make sure to keep the Lean Machean fueled and Stabilised.<br><br><span class=\"bb_img_ctn\"><img class=\"bb_img\" src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/2936620/extras/1766eaae9e401dff7888a96f672c533d.avif?t=1730941997\" width=500 height=150 /></span><br>Feeling thirsty? There's a Cuboid of Lean in the room with you that will never run out.<br>Drink from it whenever your vision starts blurring. Difficulty to focus is a sign of Dehydration.<br>Make sure not to drink too much though as Lean is highly addictive.<br><br><span class=\"bb_img_ctn\"><img class=\"bb_img\" src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/2936620/extras/c85b533568ebcbfd9d5e44d91252c857.avif?t=1730941997\" width=500 height=150 /></span><br>Thankfully, you aren't doing this for free. The Lean Monsters will pay you in Bread for giving them Lean.<br>You can use Bread to Upgrade your Lean Quality, or Output Quantity. <br>You can also use it to re-stabilise the Lean Machean in the event it destabilises too far.<br><br>You could also re-stabilise the Lean Machean manually by accessing a hatch next to it but it's recommended to save that for emergencies as you cannot defend yourself while performing Maintenance.<br><br><span class=\"bb_img_ctn\"><img class=\"bb_img\" src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/2936620/extras/1bb06c6d9e8fc583ed1899bba4c8516f.avif?t=1730941997\" width=500 height=150 /></span>:<br>PTSD is an acronym for Potential to Stack Dough, it represents how far you've come since the beginning of the game.<br>The better you perform in a single run, the more PTSD you will earn to spend on making future runs easier.<br>It is essential that you make full use of your PTSD, as you'll need to be prepared for whatever the next run might throw at you.",
